          </div>

          <p>
            For most homes the right answer is both, either as two inexpensive meters or one combination meter. Scan with a pinless meter to find the edges of the wet area, then confirm the worst spot with pins to get a number. If you can only buy one, buy a pin meter for firewood and framing, and a pinless meter if most of your use is finished surfaces like hardwood floors, painted walls and tile.
          </p>
        </div>

